				<description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;title is-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;  My dogs are my resume&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;title is-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Stress Training for Dogs&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Escape and avoidance training to teach Griz to handle stress better and listen even when no rewards are available. This is 4 sessions of forced fetch training.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/embed/SnMAGTHxG2Y?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;YouTube video&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#x9;&#x9;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;title is-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Trailing Games, Training Through Play&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Search and rescue style double blind retrieves. Two red balls (hard for dogs to see, so she has to use her nose) are placed out of sight, then Griz is cast to each one in order.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
